/*Q17. Write a Java program to search for an employee by ID using a class, constructor, an array of objects, and a member method.
Create a class named Employee with the following instance variables:
• eNo: Employee ID (an integer)
• eName: Employee Name (a string)
• eSalary: Salary of the employee (an integer)
Constructor
Implement a parameterized constructor Employee(int eNo, String eName, int eSalary) to initialize all three instance variables using the this
keyword.
Method
Implement display() in the Employee class to display the employee ID, name, and salary, each on a separate line.
The MainClass should perform the following operations:
1. Read the number of employees, N.
Ds Create an array to store N Employee objects.
35 Read the ID, name, and salary of each employee and create an Employee object for each record.
4. Read the employee ID to search for.
5 Search the array for the first employee whose ID matches the given ID.
6. If a matching employee is found, call display() for that employee and stop searching.
Ts If no matching employee is found, display "Employee not found".
Input Format:
1. The first line of input contains an integer N, representing the number of employees.
2. The next 3 x N lines each contain:
• Employee ID (integer)
• Employee Name (string)
• Employee Salary (integer)
3. The last line contains an integer representing the eNo to be searched.
Output Format:
• If the employee is found, print:
eNo
eName
eSalary
• Ifno matching employee is found, print:
Employee not found
*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
class Employee {
    int eNo;
    String eName;
    int eSalary;
 
    Employee(int eNo, String eName, int eSalary) {
        this.eNo = eNo;
        this.eName = eName;
        this.eSalary = eSalary;
    }
 
    void display() {
        System.out.println(eNo);
        System.out.println(eName);
        System.out.println(eSalary);
    }
}
 
public class MainClass {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int n = Integer.parseInt(sc.nextLine().trim());
        Employee[] emps = new Employee[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            int no = Integer.parseInt(sc.nextLine().trim());
            String name = sc.nextLine().trim();
            int sal = Integer.parseInt(sc.nextLine().trim());
            emps[i] = new Employee(no, name, sal);
        }
        int key = Integer.parseInt(sc.nextLine().trim());
        boolean found = false;
        for (Employee e : emps) {
            if (e.eNo == key) {
                e.display();
                found = true;
                break;
            }
        }
        if (!found) System.out.println("Employee not found");
        sc.close();
    }
}
